WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.336
The next morning the three children decided to walk to town.

2
00:00:06.337 --> 00:00:08.540
Soon they ran into Mabel.

3
00:00:08.541 --> 00:00:11.732
Gerald knew she was going to ask about the ring.

4
00:00:11.733 --> 00:00:15.513
Luckily they'd gotten it back from Eliza the previous night.

5
00:00:15.514 --> 00:00:18.911
Every Friday a market was set up in the square.

6
00:00:18.912 --> 00:00:27.076
Vendors sold chickens, vegetables, toys, and all sorts of interesting things.

7
00:00:27.077 --> 00:00:32.501
"Let's buy some flowers for Mademoiselle," suggested Kathleen.

8
00:00:32.502 --> 00:00:35.113
"Yes," agreed Gerald.

9
00:00:35.114 --> 00:00:38.696
"We haven't paid attention to her for the longest time."

10
00:00:38.697 --> 00:00:46.112
The children chose three bunches of carnations.

11
00:00:46.113 --> 00:00:50.162
Then they went back to the school.

12
00:00:50.163 --> 00:00:55.205
Gerald knocked on the door of the sitting room, where Mademoiselle spent all her days.

13
00:00:55.206 --> 00:00:58.401
The other children gathered behind him.

14
00:00:58.402 --> 00:01:01.717
"With love from all of us."

15
00:01:01.718 --> 00:01:05.467
Gerald gave the flowers to her.

16
00:01:05.468 --> 00:01:15.710
Mademoiselle kissed him on both cheeks.

17
00:01:15.711 --> 00:01:18.861
"What are you painting?" asked Jimmy.

18
00:01:18.862 --> 00:01:20.763
"The castle."

19
00:01:20.764 --> 00:01:24.411
"That's very good," said Mabel.

20
00:01:24.412 --> 00:01:29.045
"Are you a friend from town?" Mademoiselle asked her.

21
00:01:29.046 --> 00:01:32.047
"Actually I live at Yalding Towers,"

22
00:01:32.048 --> 00:01:35.610
said Mabel, using the castle's formal name.

23
00:01:35.611 --> 00:01:38.624
That name seemed to impress Mademoiselle.

24
00:01:38.625 --> 00:01:42.707
"Are you part of Lord Yalding's family?"

25
00:01:42.708 --> 00:01:45.286
"No, he doesn't have any family.

26
00:01:45.287 --> 00:01:46.532
He's not married.

27
00:01:46.533 --> 00:01:49.808
I'm his housekeeper's niece."

28
00:01:49.809 --> 00:01:54.556
"But you know him, don't you?" asked Mademoiselle.

29
00:01:54.557 --> 00:01:56.796
"No, I've never seen him.

30
00:01:56.797 --> 00:02:00.209
But he's supposed to be coming soon."

31
00:02:00.210 --> 00:02:02.400
"Why doesn't he live there?"

32
00:02:02.401 --> 00:02:06.418
Mademoiselle seemed very interested in this man.

33
00:02:06.419 --> 00:02:11.190
"My aunt says he's too poor," said Mabel.

34
00:02:11.191 --> 00:02:16.371
She explained that the castle had originally belonged to Lord Yalding's uncle.

35
00:02:16.372 --> 00:02:23.996
Lord Yalding had wanted to marry a woman, but his uncle had not allowed it.

36
00:02:23.997 --> 00:02:28.302
"She was a ballerina or something," explained Mabel.

37
00:02:28.303 --> 00:02:33.048
When the uncle died, he left his castle to Lord Yalding.

38
00:02:33.049 --> 00:02:35.965
But he left his money to a cousin.

39
00:02:35.966 --> 00:02:40.230
So Lord Yalding didn't have enough money to live at the castle.

40
00:02:40.231 --> 00:02:50.738
Meanwhile the woman Lord Yalding loved was sent away to a convent.

41
00:02:50.739 --> 00:02:55.336
"Did he ever try to find her?" asked Mademoiselle.

42
00:02:55.337 --> 00:03:01.162
"Oh yes," said Mabel. "But there are so many convents."

43
00:03:01.163 --> 00:03:03.528
Her eyes glowed brightly.

44
00:03:03.529 --> 00:03:08.383
"Still, I believe he will find her one day."

45
00:03:08.384 --> 00:03:12.224
Mademoiselle stared silently at Mabel.

46
00:03:12.225 --> 00:03:15.858
"My goodness!" she said finally.

47
00:03:15.859 --> 00:03:18.393
"You know a lot about Lord Yalding!

48
00:03:18.394 --> 00:03:20.283
You're a very nice girl.

49
00:03:20.284 --> 00:03:22.989
Why don't you stay for lunch?"

50
00:03:22.990 --> 00:03:29.672
Mademoiselle went out to buy some special treats.

51
00:03:29.673 --> 00:03:32.986
Jimmy and Kathleen set the dining room table.

52
00:03:32.987 --> 00:03:36.329
Gerald and Mabel were left in the sitting room.

53
00:03:36.330 --> 00:03:39.591
"You know," Gerald suddenly said.

54
00:03:39.592 --> 00:03:44.385
"It's lucky those burglars didn't go after the jewels in the treasure room."

55
00:03:44.386 --> 00:03:49.689
"I don't think anyone knows about those jewels except the four of us," said Mabel.

56
00:03:49.690 --> 00:03:55.008
"Anyway, if the burglars do know, it'll all come out at the trial."

57
00:03:55.009 --> 00:03:58.941
"There won't be a trial," said Gerald.

58
00:03:58.942 --> 00:04:00.793
"What do you mean?"

59
00:04:00.794 --> 00:04:05.367
"After I told Officer Johnson where to find the silver, I started thinking.

60
00:04:05.368 --> 00:04:07.669
I visited a prison once with my father.

61
00:04:07.670 --> 00:04:10.150
It was awful!"

62
00:04:10.151 --> 00:04:14.609
Gerald didn't want to be responsible for sending someone to prison.

63
00:04:14.610 --> 00:04:22.477
So he had left the burglars a note, warning them about the police.

64
00:04:22.478 --> 00:04:29.814
But he also said if they didn't stop stealing, he'd make sure they went to jail.

65
00:04:29.815 --> 00:04:36.028
"Speaking of stealing," said Mabel, "did you get the ring back from Eliza?"

66
00:04:36.029 --> 00:04:40.457
"Yes, but I don't know if it'll make you invisible again."

67
00:04:40.458 --> 00:04:45.503
"Why not? Did you do something to it?" Mabel asked sharply.

68
00:04:45.504 --> 00:04:49.523
"No, but it seems to be losing its powers.

69
00:04:49.524 --> 00:04:51.946
You were invisible for 21 hours.

70
00:04:51.947 --> 00:04:55.650
I was invisible for 14, and Eliza for 7.

71
00:04:55.651 --> 00:04:58.502
Next time it might not work at all."

72
00:04:58.503 --> 00:05:00.593
Mabel shook her head.

73
00:05:00.594 --> 00:05:08.636
"We don't understand the mystery of that ring yet."

